{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Snapshot recovery exposes a more concrete discriminator: when an installed snapshot has the same index as the follower’s cached last log, `getLastEntry` prefers the cached log’s term. Installation updates the snapshot boundary but leaves that cache unchanged. I’ll test whether an accepted snapshot can therefore be followed by rejection of an append that correctly names its boundary.\n"}}
